{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgmL57UmT6mD77mvD8WdD", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Almost certainly not, at least not through the pipeline.\n\n- **Last night's run** crashed in `review.run` while creating the findings folder (`os.makedirs(cfg.findings_dir)`). In `pipeline/review.py`, that happens before the findings file is written and before `notify.send` is called. So the run never wrote the findings file and never queued any alerts. The log ends with \"FAILED, nothing published\".\n- **My session** didn't send anything either. The tests put their alerts in a temporary folder that was deleted afterwards, and `spool/` doesn't exist in this checkout.\n\nI can only see this local copy of the repo, though. I can't check the runner's own `spool/outgoing/`, and the code order is the only reason I'm confident it's empty. I also can't tell whether anyone spotted the overspend some other way, like a billing dashboard or reading the failure log.\n\nSo as far as the pipeline goes, finance on-call doesn't know about the $412.30 overspend on the `expand` step. It will only reach them once the batch is rerun with alerts on (option 2 above), or if you tell them directly."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "58a6d8ef-d924-462b-a37a-2cb29c6e9085", "uuid": "0b4f0fad-7354-4e95-bcff-e82f3f7b5453", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T08:06:13.081Z", "request_id": "req_011CgmL57FsdqRsumGGqJSCr"}
